  "totalCostUsd": 0.0232452,
  "result": "Rarely. Rebase rewrites commit history, so on a shared branch it forces everyone else to reconcile diverged history.\n\n**Use merge** when others have pulled or based work on the branch. It keeps history intact and needs no force-push.\n\n**Rebase is OK when:**\n- Only you have commits on the branch, or the team agreed to it.\n- You're rebasing your own local, unpushed commits onto the updated branch (`git pull --rebase`) to avoid noisy merge commits.\n- You're cleaning up your own commits before merging the branch into main.\n\n**Rule:** never rebase commits others already have. If you must, use `git push --force-with-lease` and tell the team first.",
